1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,820
Johnstown, Pennsylvania.
May 31, 1889.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:11,370
14 miles upstream, a lake sat
behind a wall of packed earth.

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,320
The wall was 72 feet high.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,420
Cut it open, and you see the problem:

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,910
60 feet of water, held back by dirt.

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:26,620
At about 3:10 p.m.,
the dam gave way.

7
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,570
20 million tons of water
poured down the valley,

8
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,920
a wave 35 feet high at its crest.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,120
At 4:07 p.m., it hit Johnstown.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:42,470
At the Stone Bridge, the wreckage
piled 40 feet high, and caught fire.

11
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:46,805
2,209 people died.
